{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"The root cause was a password mismatch for the Postgres role `otelu`. I reset the role's password and submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned 200.\n\n`product-catalog` and `product-reviews` connect as `otelu` with the password in their config. Postgres rejected that password (\"password authentication failed for user otelu\"), so product-catalog kept crashing. The frontend errors were all downstream of that.\n\nThe fix was `ALTER ROLE otelu WITH LOGIN PASSWORD 'otelp_7k9m2q4x'`, matching the password in the `product-catalog-db-conn` secret and the `product-reviews` deployment. I then restarted `product-catalog`, `product-reviews` and `frontend`.\n\nAfter the restart, `product-catalog` shows no errors and `product-reviews` is returning review data from the database. I didn't get a direct end-to-end check of the storefront. The `wget` test inside the frontend pod failed because the image doesn't have it. The frontend log lines I checked afterwards were from startup, before `product-catalog` was up."}}
